From abea5b4e9fbd1d35be286346e054d895e309c6a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:37:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] e-ink: weather and next event in the sleep screen's bottom
 corners

EinkSleepScreen draws two optional corners, both set up in HiBreakParts
(Settings > Display > E-ink & front light > Sleep screen), which writes
them to Settings.System for SystemUI:
- bottom left, hibreak_sleep_weather_data: a weather icon, the
  temperature in C or F and the city below. The icons are line drawings
  in the text colour (EinkWeatherIcon: clear and partly cloudy by day and
  night, cloudy, fog, drizzle, rain, snow, thunder), no grey for the
  one-bit panel. Not shown when the data is over 12 hours old.
- bottom right, hibreak_sleep_calendar_data: the next event's title (up
  to two lines) and when ("Today 14:00", "Tomorrow 09:30", "Thu 10:00",
  "Today 14:00-15:00" while it runs, the day alone for all-day events).
  Not shown once it has ended.
Both are read at every redraw, so a change shows at the next minute
tick. With either corner shown the battery moves to the top.
